    <div class="wrap" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px;max-width:760px;align-items:center;text-align:center;">
      <div class="ds-label eyebrow-c">Agent First Labs &middot; 3-round race</div>
      <h1 class="ds-display" style="color:#fff;">Can You Beat Agent First?</h1>
      <p class="ds-body" style="color:#c7cce0;">Three rounds. The same three fictional clients you have seen throughout this site. Somewhere in a shared knowledge base, sorted by topic instead of by client, is the exact rule you need. Find it, pick it, and see how your time compares to Agent First matching the call to a Client Profile and the active rule, automatically.</p>
      <div class="grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(200px,1fr));margin-top:8px;width:100%;">
        <div class="card-on-dark">
          <div class="ds-body" style="font-weight:750;color:#fff;margin-bottom:4px;">One shared knowledge base</div>
          <div class="ds-body-sm" style="color:#c7cce0;">Four topics, three clients each: twelve lines total, sorted by topic the way most internal documentation actually is, not sorted for you.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="card-on-dark">
          <div class="ds-body" style="font-weight:750;color:#fff;margin-bottom:4px;">This is not a live AI guessing</div>
          <div class="ds-body-sm" style="color:#c7cce0;">What races you here is the same deterministic client-and-topic match described throughout this site, animated at roughly the speed a lookup like that actually takes. Nothing invented, nothing hidden.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="card-on-dark">
          <div class="ds-body" style="font-weight:750;color:#fff;margin-bottom:4px;">Speed and accuracy, tracked separately</div>
          <div class="ds-body-sm" style="color:#c7cce0;">Answer first with the wrong client's rule and you still lose the round on accuracy. Both get counted, then shown to you honestly at the end.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <button class="btn btn-primary" id="startBtn" style="margin-top:6px;padding:15px 34px;font-size:16px;">Start the race</button>
      <p class="ds-body-sm" style="color:#8991b3;">Works best on a laptop or desktop screen. Nothing is recorded or sent anywhere. This runs entirely in your browser.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

