        <a href="client-roulette.html" class="btn btn-ghost-light">Try the faster version: Client Roulette</a>
        <a href="agent-challenge.html" class="btn btn-ghost-light">Try the original: Agent Challenge</a>
      </div>

      <div class="card-on-dark" style="flex-direction:column;gap:14px;background:var(--navy);border:none;display:flex;">
        <div class="ds-body" style="font-weight:900;color:#fff;">Agent First was not guessing. It was matching.</div>
        <p class="ds-body-sm" style="color:#c7cce0;">Every round, Agent First's side resolved the same way: match the call to a Client Profile, match the request to the active rule, apply it. No search, no scrolling, no chance of grabbing the wrong client's line by accident. See what that looks like against your own rules.</p>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
